+get_llm() returns a FallbackChat: it exposes the same three methods the
+orchestrator uses (bind_tools / astream / ainvoke) but tries the primary
+provider first and moves on to LLM_FALLBACK_n_* when a call fails with a
+rate limit (429), provider error (5xx), timeout, connection error, or a
+retired/unknown model.
+
+Note: failover happens BEFORE the first token is streamed. If a provider
+dies halfway through an answer, that error propagates as before (and the
+widgets already keep whatever text streamed) - we never splice two models'
+output into one reply.
